  "h1": "Best DataAnnotation Alternatives for AI Training Work",
  "introText": "The best [DataAnnotation](https://www.dataannotation.tech/faqs) alternatives for remote AI training work are [Outlier](https://outlier.ai/faq), [Mercor](https://talent.docs.mercor.com/how-to/payments), [Alignerr](https://www.alignerr.com/), [Mindrift](https://mindrift.ai/), [Handshake AI](https://support.joinhandshake.com/hc/en-us/articles/32264709473303) and [Prolific](https://www.prolific.com/ai-taskers).\n\nAt ModernWallet, every guide we write starts from the platform's own published rules and pay pages. DataAnnotation's [Trustpilot reviews](https://www.trustpilot.com/review/dataannotation.tech) list long stretches with no available work and balances held during account review among the recurring complaints. A second platform gives you somewhere to work when one queue is empty.",
  "rankingCriteria": "Each option is compared on four factors: pay transparency, payout method and schedule, entry requirements, and track record. Pay transparency means a published hourly range rather than pay set per project or listing. Track record covers lawsuits, settlements, regulator actions and data breaches found on court dockets and in named news reports. The platforms are listed in order of how directly their workflow replaces DataAnnotation's mix of general and coding task work, rather than as a quality ranking.",
  "options": [
    {
      "name": "Outlier",
      "bestFor": "Workers wanting prompt evaluation with weekly Tuesday payouts",
      "description": "Outlier is an AI training platform operated by Scale AI. Contributors generate prompts, rank AI outputs, improve model responses, or complete other tasks on the platform. The platform does not publish an hourly rate on its FAQ; it says task rates vary by expertise, project complexity, and location, and are shown before starting each project. Payouts process weekly on Tuesdays for work completed Tuesday through Monday via PayPal, Airtm, or ACH bank transfer. Getting started requires an associate degree, resume, LinkedIn profile, valid identification, and a 30 to 90 minute onboarding process. In December 2024, contributors filed a class action alleging worker misclassification, resulting in a proposed $12.5 million settlement currently awaiting final approval on October 30, 2026.",
      "strengths": [
        "Offers weekly payouts processed on Tuesdays via PayPal, Airtm, or ACH bank transfer",
        "Shows task rates to contributors before starting any specific project",
        "Covers diverse tasks including prompt generation and model response evaluation",
        "Open to contributors holding at least an associate degree"
      ],
